From: mckenna654 <mckenna654@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:11:12 +1100
Subject: fix: the battle box no longer flashes white when the buttons come
 back

Drawing the buttons takes several frames of the console's time. The menu asked
for the message window to be copied to the screen before drawing, so the next
frames showed the half-drawn box in the message box's colours: a white flash
with part of the first button in it, every turn. Now nothing is sent until the
picture is finished.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CNqSDphYuD2Aqe9TExdQMP

diff --git a/src/little_trainers_battle_ui.c b/src/little_trainers_battle_ui.c
index 8d2d221fc..43f4cf652 100644
--- a/src/little_trainers_battle_ui.c
+++ b/src/little_trainers_battle_ui.c
@@ -345,7 +345,12 @@ void LT_BattleMenu_Show(u8 battler)
     if (!SlotShown(gActionSelectionCursor[battler]))
         gActionSelectionCursor[battler] = LT_MENU_ATTACK;
 
-    BattlePutTextOnWindow(gText_EmptyString3, B_WIN_MSG);
+    // Stop any message still being printed in this window, but do not send the window to the
+    // screen yet. Drawing the buttons takes several frames of the console's time, and a copy
+    // asked for now would be carried out at the next frame: the box would show whatever had been
+    // drawn so far, in the message box's colours (a white flash with part of a button in it).
+    // The one copy at the end sends the finished picture and its colours together.
+    BattlePutTextOnWindow(gText_EmptyString3, B_WIN_MSG | B_TEXT_FLAG_WINDOW_CLEAR); // (the flag means: leave the window alone)
     LoadPalette(sIconsPal, BG_PLTT_ID(MENU_PALETTE), PLTT_SIZE_4BPP);
     sPulseTimer = 0;
 
